    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.invert_edge_selection - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.invert_edge_selection.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.invert_edge_selection()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Invert edge selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.invert_edge_selection()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Invert edge selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.invert_edge_selection()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Invert edge selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nInvert edge selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L30495-L30569){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.invert_edge_selection()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Invert edge selection](../assets/graphs/invert-edge-selection.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Before: edges A–B, B–E, and E–F are selected in the accent color. After invert_edge_selection the selection flips: the other four edges are selected and those three are plain.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nReplaces the edge selection with its complement: every currently selected edge becomes\nunselected and every unselected edge becomes selected. With no edges selected, the result\nis that all edges are selected.\n\nThis is the edge counterpart of `invert_node_selection()` and is handy for \"keep only\"\noperations -- select the edges to keep, invert, then `delete_edges_ws()` -- or for\napplying an attribute to every edge *except* a chosen few with `set_edge_attrs_ws()`.\nAny node selection is cleared, since the graph holds a selection of nodes or of edges but\nnot both. The graph is modified in place and returned for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The same graph (modified in place) for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~invert_node_selection`) \n\n:   Select the nodes that aren't selected.\n\n[](`~deselect_edges`) \n\n:   Remove edges from the selection.\n\n[](`~delete_edges_ws`) \n\n:   Delete the selected edges.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nSelecting one edge of a cycle and inverting the selection leaves the other four:\n\n::: {#d1b0664a .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(5)\ngraph.select_edges_by_id([1]).invert_edge_selection()\n\ngraph.count_selected_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n4\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Keeping only the large payments\n\n`payments()` is a month of payments between 18 accounts at a made-up bank, each directed\nfrom payer to payee. To keep only the payments of 1,000 or more, select them, invert the\nselection to get the small ones and delete those:\n\n::: {#04aef30c .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments = ec.payments()\n(\n    payments\n    .select_edges(lambda e: e.attributes[\"amount\"] >= 1000)\n    .invert_edge_selection()\n    .delete_edges_ws()\n)\n\npayments.count_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n16\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWhat is left falls into two parts. In one, Acme pays the salaries, Max pays the rent and\nEve's money goes on to the loop through Finn, Gus and Hal. In the other, money goes\naround Ana, Ben and Cruz, and on along the chain to Lena. The Grocer and the Cafe are\nleft with no payments at all:\n\n::: {#b742fa90 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments.plot(label_by=\"label\", seed=3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-hig